from pathlib import Path
import html,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P=R.parent
load=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
d=load(R/'RESULTS.json');q=load(R/'QUALIFICATION.json');chain=load(R/'LOCAL-CHAIN-COUNTEREXAMPLE.json');e=lambda v:html.escape(str(v))
def table(h,rs):return '<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(v)+'</th>' for v in h)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+str(v)+'</td>' for v in r)+'</tr>' for r in rs)+'</tbody></table></div>'
body='<p class="muted">VOYNICH · ONE-WORD-GAP ORDER · v78</p><h1>Does sh- precede qok- with one word between?</h1><p class="notice">This is a distance-extension test, not a grammar-versus-junction detector. Gap survival can arise from chained local transitions; gap failure cannot prove a boundary mechanism. The earlier adjacent-order result is preserved.</p>'
body+='<p>Exactly three consecutive readable source tokens: <code>sh-word · middle word · qok-word</code>, versus reverse endpoints. No crossing of lines, unknown slots or invented token joins. Bath hand2/B/P and Starred hand3/B/P only, H/F separate and original shared source loci unchanged. “Starred paragraphs” is the tested section; it is not the separately labelled Recipes section.</p>'
body+='<h2>Qualified before manuscript gap scoring</h2><p>New gap counters and both middle definitions passed independent literal counts across 72 authored exact line-permutation arrangements (144 view checks). The unchanged maxT method was rechecked for the doubled correction across all eight earlier numerical banks before any corpus gap scores.</p>'
body+=table(['Bank','Null rotation flags /4096','Attainable adjusted p','Worst 8-SD plant hits /64','All gates'],[[b['bank'],str(b['null_flags'])+'/4096',f'{max(b["minimum_adjusted_p"]):.6f}',str(min(x['hits'] for x in b['strong_power']))+'/64','PASS' if b['passes'] else 'FAIL'] for b in q['banks']])
body+='<p>These numerical views reuse correlated control banks; they are not independent historical or semantic tests. Qualification covers implementation, finite-row rank calibration and strong planted sensitivity under those controls. It does not establish power for every possible language or syntactic relation.</p>'
body+='<p><a href="VIEW-UNION-BOUND.json">Two-view dependence audit:</a> each bank has a worst-case union-bound ceiling of 196 rejecting rows out of 4096, below the 204-row gate, regardless of dependence between the two definitions. Duplicating bank views alone is not a worst-case dependence simulation; the arithmetic union bound supplies that guarantee. This clarifies the frozen protocol wording without changing any score or gate.</p>'
body+='<h2>One-word-gap results</h2>'
body+=table(['Section / hand','Reading','Middle definition','Forward / reverse','Observed D','Null mean D','95% null range','Regularized Z','Opening-family p','Full x28 p'],[[e(p['section']+' / '+p['hand']),p['reading'],e(p['view']),str(p['cells']['forward'])+'/'+str(p['cells']['reverse']),p['result']['observed_D'],f'{p["result"]["null_mean"]:.3f}',e(p['result']['null_95']),f'{p["result"]["observed_Z"]:.3f}',f'{p["result"]["p_family"]:.4f}',f'{p["result"]["p_all_panels"]:.4f}'] for p in d['panels']])
passes=[p['section']+' '+p['hand']+' '+p['reading']+' '+p['view'] for p in d['panels'] if p['result']['observed_Z']>0 and p['result']['p_all_panels']<=.05]
body+='<p class="notice"><strong>Positive direction passing the full screen:</strong> '+e('; '.join(passes) or 'none')+'. Every nonpassing, zero and reverse outcome remains recorded. Absence of a gap finding does not undo the adjacent finding or identify its cause.</p>'
body+='<p><strong>any_middle:</strong> every readable middle word, including sh-/qok- words. <strong>non_target_middle:</strong> fixed sensitivity excluding intervening sh-/qok- words, with that filter recomputed in every shuffle. This exposes repeated runs such as sh sh qok. H/F tokenization is not silently aligned: one token gap need not mean the same glyph span in both readings.</p>'
body+='<h2>Null and unchanged search family</h2><p>4,999 fresh within-line shuffles per reading/stratum, shared between the two middle definitions. Each line retains its own words, endpoints and unknown barriers. Every original eligible prefix pair remains in the end-opening search family; both directions enter count-unit-regularized maxT.</p><p>The original 14-panel correction is retained and doubled for the two definitions: x28, despite scoring only four reading/stratum panels here. Only lag2 was tested; no search for a winning gap distance. Adjacent lag1 results remain reference measurements with their original x14 correction, not new hypotheses folded into this run.</p>'
old=load(P/'opening-maxT-qualification-v77/RESULTS.json');ids={p['original_panel_index'] for p in d['panels']}
body+='<details><summary>Preserved adjacent-order reference · original x14 correction</summary>'+table(['Section','Hand','Reading','Forward / reverse','Original adjusted p'],[[e(p['section']),p['hand'],p['reading'],str(p['rules'][0]['forward'])+'/'+str(p['rules'][0]['reverse']),f'{p["rules"][0]["p_all_panels"]:.4f}'] for p in old['panels'] if p['panel_index'] in ids])+'</details>'
body+='<h2>Why a gap is not a decisive mechanism test</h2><p>A predefined five-state first-order control uses only the current token: shaa chooses qokbb or m; m→qokbb→r→t→shaa. It has no nonlocal state or look-back. Yet it generates both the adjacent and one-gap preferences:</p>'+table(['Distance','Forward','Reverse'],[[lag,x['forward'],x['reverse']] for lag,x in chain['counts'].items()])
body+='<p>This is a logical counterexample, not a fitted model of the manuscript or proof of a character-junction mechanism. It shows that neighbour-to-neighbour effects can propagate over an intervening word. Conversely, a grammatical relation can require adjacency, so its disappearance at a gap would not prove a junction cause.</p><p>Discriminating structure beyond first-order transitions would require an independently qualified control that preserves or explicitly models local transitions. That stronger null was not run here.</p>'
body+='<h2>Middle words, reverse examples and folio exceptions</h2>'
for o in d['observed']:
 body+='<details><summary>'+e(o['section']+' · hand '+o['hand']+' · '+o['reading'])+'</summary><p>Candidate endpoint pairs excluded because middle slot was unknown: '+str(o['unknown_middle_excluded'])+'. Unknown slots were not promoted to words.</p>'+table(['Folio','Any forward','Any reverse','Other-middle forward','Other-middle reverse'],[[e(f),x['forward'],x['reverse'],x['neutral_forward'],x['neutral_reverse']] for f,x in sorted(o['folios'].items())])
 body+='<details><summary>Every middle word</summary>'+table(['Written middle','Forward','Reverse','Target-type middle?'],[[e(w),x.get('forward',0),x.get('reverse',0),'yes' if w.startswith(('sh','qok')) else 'no'] for w,x in o['middle_words'].items()])+'</details>'
 for orientation in ['reverse','forward']:
  body+='<details><summary>All '+orientation+' source triples</summary>'
  for ev in o['events']:
   if ev['orientation']!=orientation:continue
   i=ev['ordinal']-1;body+='<article><p><strong>'+e(ev['locator'])+'</strong> · ordinal '+str(ev['ordinal'])+' · '+('non-target middle' if ev['neutral_middle'] else 'sh/qok middle: omitted from sensitivity')+'</p><p class="raw">'+' '.join('□' if w is None else '<mark>'+e(w)+'</mark>' if j in (i,i+1,i+2) else e(w) for j,w in enumerate(ev['tokens']))+'</p></article>'
  body+='</details>'
 body+='</details>'
body+='<h2>Limits retained</h2><p>The corpus was already inspected. H/F are alternative readings, not independent datasets. Two identified scribes agreeing does not eliminate shared conventions, copying or common training. The within-line null controls per-line vocabulary and endpoints, not every exact interior position. Botanical hand5’s earlier tie is not a positive directional finding. No word meanings or operation/attribute/timing labels follow from either distance test.</p><p><a href="RESULTS.json">All gap results and source cases</a> · <a href="PROTOCOL.json">Frozen lag and middle definitions</a> · <a href="QUALIFICATION.json">Pre-scoring qualification</a> · <a href="LOCAL-CHAIN-COUNTEREXAMPLE.json">Local-chain counterexample</a> · <a href="VERIFICATION.json">Numerical checks</a> · <a href="../opening-maxT-qualification-v77/report.html">Preserved adjacent result</a></p><p>Browser appearance unreviewed; source and numerical verification are separate.</p>'
css='''<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark;--bg:light-dark(#f5f2e9,#18251f);--fg:light-dark(#203f35,#e2e9df);--sub:light-dark(#54695b,#b4c7b7);--rule:light-dark(#c0ccbd,#48604d);--fill:light-dark(#e5ebda,#2a3e2d);--mark:light-dark(#e6edb7,#526330)}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui}main{max-width:1450px;padding:30px;margin:auto}h1{font-size:32px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:23px;margin-top:30px}p{max-width:1100px}a{color:inherit}.muted{color:var(--sub)}.notice{padding:16px;background:var(--fill)}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:9px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}.raw{font:15px/1.8 ui-monospace,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}mark{background:var(--mark);color:inherit}article{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)}summary{cursor:pointer}details{margin:16px 0}@media(max-width:700px){main{padding:16px}}</style>'''
(R/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>One-word-gap opening order · v78</title>'+css+'</head><body><main>'+body+'</main></body></html>',encoding='utf-8');print('Gap report written with middle/folio exceptions and mechanism limits.')
